  "content_html": "\n        <figure style=\"margin: 24px 0;\">\n            <img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1768853099411-b0405e07c73d?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3wxMDY2MTU3fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8bGFyZ2UlMjBnYWxsb24lMjB3YXRlciUyMGJvdHRsZSUyMHNpdHRpbmclMjBvbiUyMGElMjBraXRjaGVuJTIwY291bnRlcnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzg5NDQ1ODQ0fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080\" alt=\"Oz To Gallon - Clear glass pitcher with water on a countertop\" style=\"width: 100%; max-height: 480px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 8px;\" />\n        </figure>\n        <h2>How Many Ounces Are in a Gallon? Quick Answer</h2>\n\n<p><strong>There are exactly 128 US fluid ounces in 1 US liquid gallon. To convert fluid ounces to gallons, divide your total ounce figure by 128.</p>\n<div class=\"gp-interactive-tool-box\" id=\"gp-general-calculator\">\n    <div class=\"gp-tool-header\">\n        <h3 class=\"gp-tool-title\">\n            <svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 6v6l4 2\"/></svg>\n            Interactive Oz To Gallon Decision Tool\n        </h3>\n        <span class=\"gp-tool-badge\">Decision Tool</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"gp-tool-grid\">\n        <div class=\"gp-tool-group\">\n            <label class=\"gp-tool-label\">Baseline Amount ($)</label>\n            <input type=\"number\" id=\"gp-gen-base\" class=\"gp-tool-input\" value=\"5000\" oninput=\"runGeneralCalc()\">\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"gp-tool-group\">\n            <label class=\"gp-tool-label\">Adjustment Rate (%)</label>\n            <input type=\"number\" id=\"gp-gen-rate\" class=\"gp-tool-input\" value=\"7.5\" step=\"0.5\" oninput=\"runGeneralCalc()\">\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"gp-tool-group\">\n            <label class=\"gp-tool-label\">Timeline (Years / Terms)</label>\n            <input type=\"number\" id=\"gp-gen-years\" class=\"gp-tool-input\" value=\"3\" min=\"1\" max=\"50\" oninput=\"runGeneralCalc()\">\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"gp-tool-results\">\n        <div class=\"gp-result-item\">\n            <span class=\"gp-result-label\">Projected Outcome</span>\n            <span class=\"gp-result-value\" id=\"gp-gen-total\">$6,211</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"gp-result-item\">\n            <span class=\"gp-result-label\">Net Variance</span>\n            <span class=\"gp-result-value\" style=\"color: #10b981;\" id=\"gp-gen-diff\">+$1,211</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"gp-result-item\">\n            <span class=\"gp-result-label\">Annualized Return</span>\n            <span class=\"gp-result-value\" style=\"font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-main);\" id=\"gp-gen-annual\">$2,070 / yr</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"gp-tool-note\">Live interactive projection utility for <strong>Oz To Gallon</strong>.</p>\n</div>\n<script>\nfunction runGeneralCalc() {\n    var base = parseFloat(document.getElementById('gp-gen-base').value) || 0;\n    var rate = (parseFloat(document.getElementById('gp-gen-rate').value) || 0) / 100;\n    var yrs = parseFloat(document.getElementById('gp-gen-years').value) || 1;\n\n    var total = base * Math.pow(1 + rate, yrs);\n    var diff = total - base;\n    var annual = yrs > 0 ? (total / yrs) : total;\n\n    document.getElementById('gp-gen-total').innerText = \"$\" + Math.round(total).toLocaleString();\n    document.getElementById('gp-gen-diff').innerText = (diff >= 0 ? \"+$\" : \"-$\") + Math.round(Math.abs(diff)).toLocaleString();\n    document.getElementById('gp-gen-annual').innerText = \"$\" + Math.round(annual).toLocaleString() + \" / yr\";\n}\nrunGeneralCalc();\n</script>\n\n\n<p>For UK Imperial measurements, 1 Imperial gallon contains 160 Imperial fluid ounces, which equals roughly 153.72 US fluid ounces.</strong></p>\n\n<p>Liquid volume conversions catch people off guard because the word \"ounce\" describes two completely different things. Fluid ounces quantify liquid volume, while dry ounces quantify gravitational weight.</p>\n        <figure class=\"mid-article-figure\" style=\"margin: 36px 0;\">\n            <img src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1780884864610-37a3837d1bb3?crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&fit=max&fm=jpg&ixid=M3wxMDY2MTU3fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8bGFyZ2UlMjBnYWxsb24lMjB3YXRlciUyMGJvdHRsZSUyMHNpdHRpbmclMjBvbiUyMGElMjBraXRjaGVuJTIwY291bnRlcnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzg5NDQ1ODQ0fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&w=1080\" alt=\"Oz To Gallon - A pastry under a glass cloche on a wooden board\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"width: 100%; max-height: 480px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 8px;\" />\n        </figure>\n        \n\n<p><p>When measuring liquids, always confirm you are working with liquid fluid ounces rather than dry ounces. Kitchen scales calculate dry weight, which will</p>",
